tice-in-kelly-country-the-story-of-the-cop-who-hunted-australia-s-most-notorious-bushrangers-","book-kinglake-350-adrian-hyland","book-light-of-the-stars-alien-worlds-and-the-fate-of-the-earth-adam-frank","book-the-premonitions-bureau-a-true-account-of-death-foretold-sam-knight","book-american-revolutions-a-continental-history-1750-1804-alan-taylor","book-climate-injustice-friederike-otto","book-intertidal-yuvan-aves","book-island-on-fire-the-extraordinary-story-of-a-forgotten-volcano-that-changed-the-world-alexandra-w"],"pageCount":452},"appearances":[{"id":"appearance-the-cultural-revolution-a-people-s-history-1962-1976-frank-dikotter-pen-hessell-tiltman-prize-historical-nonfiction-2017-shortlist","bookId":"book-the-cultural-revolution-a-people-s-history-1962-1976-frank-dikotter","awardId":"award-pen-hessell-tiltman-prize-historical-nonfiction","awardEditionId":"edition-pen-hessell-tiltman-prize-historical-nonfiction-2017","year":2017,"status":"shortlist","originalStatus":"shortlist","statusRank":3,"isTie":false,"sourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/PEN_Hessell-Tiltman_Prize","sourceIds":["source-award-record-hessell-tiltman-history-wikipedia-pen-hessell-tiltman-prize-winners-and-shortlists"],"award":{"awardType":"award","name":"PEN Hessell-Tiltman Prize: Historical Nonfiction","slug":"pen-hessell-tiltman-prize-historical-nonfiction"},"statusLabel":"Shortlist"}],"imprint":"Bloomsbury","publisher":"Bloomsbury Publishing","stats":{"bookId":"book-the-cultural-revolution-a-people-s-history-1962-1976-frank-dikotter","wins":0,"lists":1,"score":2,"majorWins":0,"normalWins":0,"majorShortlists":0,"normalShortlists":1,"majorLonglists":0,"normalLonglists":0,"statuses":{"winner":0,"co_winner":0,"finalist":0,"shortlist":1,"longlist":0,"honorable_mention":0,"commended":0,"notable":0,"unknown":0}},"wikipediaEvidence":{"bookId":"book-the-cultural-revolution-a-people-s-history-1962-1976-frank-dikotter","pageTitle":"The Cultural Revolution: A People's History, 1962–1976","pageId":80665399,"wikidataId":"Q97300318","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Cultural_Revolution%3A_A_People's_History%2C_1962%E2%80%931976","revisionId":1356505470,"accessedAt":"2026-08-03T19:00:12.125Z","extract":"The Cultural Revolution: A People's History, 1962–1976 is a book by University of Hong Kong historian Frank Dikötter. It is the third book in a trilogy about the history of China under Mao Zedong, based on newly opened government archives, particularly on previously classified party documents from secret police reports and unexpurgated versions of leadership speeches, as well as on interviews and memoirs. Dikötter's first book in the series, Mao's Great Famine, covered the period of the Great Leap Forward, whereas The Tragedy of Liberation examines the establishment and first decade of the People's Republic of China. After the failure of the Great Leap Forward, Mao Zedong launched the Cultural Revolution to restore his reputation and eliminate perceived threats. Aimed at purging capitalist and bourgeois elements, it mobilized youth into Red Guards who initially supported Mao but soon turned on each other violently. The resulting chaos led to military intervention, transforming China into a militarised state and triggering large-scale purges in which as many as one in fifty people were crushed. In the book, Dikötter discusses the causes and consequences of the Cultural Revolution and provides a crucial reminder of the tragedies, miscalculations and human costs of Mao's last experiment.","matchedBy":"infobox_book:high","confidence":"high","attribution":{"label":"Wikipedia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Cultural_Revolution%3A_A_People's_History%2C_1962%E2%80%931976","license":"CC BY-SA","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/"},"infobox":{"title":"The Cultural Revolution: A People's History, 1962–1976","author":"Frank Dikötter","publisher":"Bloomsbury Press","publicationDate":"2016","pages":"452","isbn":"978-1-63286-421-5"